import"./chunk-GAL4ENT6.js";var s="# Vanilla RxJS\n\nA contest entry: plain RxJS, as it ships with Angular. No data library, no\nstore, no `@rx-evo/stateful-observable`. Judged by the page tests\n(`PAGE_TARGET=vanilla-rxjs npm test`) and the e2e suite\n(`E2E_CONTESTER=vanilla-rxjs npm run e2e`).\n\nStatus: see [test_report.md](test_report.md), regenerated by `npm run test:report`.\nThe machinery built by hand: [gaps.md](gaps.md).\n\n## Extra code\n\nCode that is not about the page's domain: caches, batching, status mapping,\nlifetime, written per entity or as generic helpers. Lines from\n[card 06](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/06-boilerplate.md) (Prettier-formatted, non-blank, non-comment), compared with\nthe four entries (vanilla-rxjs, ngrx-signal-store, resources,\nstateful-observable).\n\n| Measure | Lines | vs average | vs best | vs worst |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Extra code (generic + per-entity) | **595** | +53% vs average (388) | +406 vs best | worst |\n| Whole data layer | **1668** | +99% vs average (840) | +1367 vs best | worst |\n| One more batched lookup like `tiers` | **20** | +4% vs average (19) | +7 vs best | \u221210 vs worst |\n\n## Idea\n\nThe data layer is two caches and one store, all in `data/`:\n\n- `query.ts`: a keyed read. One `Entry` per key, shared by every observer of\n  it. The first observer starts the request; the last one to leave cancels a\n  request still in flight; a settled value stays cached. Options: `pollMs`\n  (refetch while observed) and `keepOnError` (keep the last data on failure).\n- `entity-cache.ts`: a per-id read for the services that take ids. Ids asked\n  in the same tick are collected, split into chunks of at most `MAX_BATCH`,\n  and each id gets one slot. A failed batch turns only its own ids into\n  `error`; a service without a batch endpoint gets one call per id.\n- `sources.ts`: every query and cache of the console, and `clearSession()`,\n  which forgets everything bound to the user. Products, prices, stock and the\n  product search are public and survive logout.\n- `console.store.ts`: the one injectable the console reads from. It holds one\n  stream per section (`signedIn$`-gated), the writes with their\n  invalidations, and the retry paths.\n- `raw-models.ts`, `mappers.ts`, `vm.ts`: DTO to view model. Inside the store a\n  row keeps the pieces other services enrich it with as `Fetched`, so \"failed\"\n  and \"not yet\" stay distinct. `withParts` enriches a section once per new\n  value. A failed enrichment is a notice on a ready section (`flag`), not a\n  hidden field.\n- `block-state.ts`, `fetched.ts`, `view-state.ts`: what a section's block gets\n  (`loading`, `error`, `data`).\n\nField components read one stream per value from the store and take no lookup\ninput from their parents.\n\n## Good\n\n- Every behaviour is an operator at the place it belongs: `switchMap` for\n  latest-wins and for logout (`signedIn$`), `debounceTime` for the search\n  (R-L4), `finalize` for cancellation when the last observer leaves (R-C4),\n  `combineLatest` only where a section needs more than one stream (R-P5).\n- Nothing subscribes until a view asks (R-L2): streams are cold until\n  observed, and a section that is not shown sends no request.\n- A failure stays in its section: each section is its own stream, so one\n  failing source does not block the rest (R-G3, R-P1).\n\n## Bad\n\nOnly failing requirements and the excess code they cost (spec \xA711):\n\n- **Caching, sharing and batching are hand-written.** `query.ts` (119 lines)\n  and `entity-cache.ts` (136 lines) hold the bookkeeping for R-L3, R-L5, R-L9\n  and R-L10: slots, observer counts, batch windows and stale flags. It is the\n  largest single cost of the entry; [gaps.md](gaps.md) lists all the\n  hand-built machinery, the baseline the other entries are compared with.\n- **Retry is per source by hand.** `retryCustomerSource` switches over six\n  keys and calls `retryIfFailed` or `retryFailed` for each, to meet R-G5 (only\n  what failed is asked again).\n- **Error notices are plumbing.** `failedCalls`, `flag` and `keepPrevious` in\n  `vm.ts` carry the raw errors of enrichments and of stale data to the\n  views, for R-E1, R-G2, R-G6 and R-C3.\n- **Write guards are explicit.** `write()` checks `pending` for R-W2 and an\n  `epoch` for R-W5 and R-W8 (a response from a previous session is dropped).\n\nNothing fails in the current run (102 page tests, 104 e2e). The B10 e2e failure of an earlier run (\"execution context was destroyed\") did not come back.\n\n## Requirements\n\n| Requirement | How it is met |\n| --- | --- |\n| R-S1 | helper: `signedIn$` gates every private stream (`console.store.ts`) |\n| R-S2 | helper: the agent and notifications streams start with the session (`console.store.ts`) |\n| R-S3 | built in: `switchMap` on `signedIn$` drops every private view at once |\n| R-S4 | helper: `clearSession()` in `sources.ts` forgets every user-bound cache |\n| R-S5 | helper: the tab preference is kept in the store across navigation (`console.store.ts`) |\n| R-D1 | built in: each section is a `Query`/`EntityCache` observer for its own key |\n| R-D2 | helper: `pollMs` in `query.ts` (notifications, activity) |\n| R-B1 | helper: `app-view-block` fed by `block-state.ts` |\n| R-J1 | helper: names and prices are their own streams (`raw-models.ts`), never shown as unresolved |\n| R-J2 | helper: the mappers in `mappers.ts` pick the field each view takes |\n| R-J3 | helper: `entity-cache.ts` chunks ids at `MAX_BATCH` |\n| R-J4 | helper: cart and hit prices come from the `prices` cache for the current sku |\n| R-J5 | helper: the linked ticket is found in `ticketsByOrder` (`vm.ts`) |\n| R-J6 | not in the data layer: sentences are written by the shared views from kind and refs |\n| R-J7 | helper: each counter has one `EntityCache` (`ticketCounts`, `orderStats`) |\n| R-C1 | built in: `switchMap` on the input, and `Query` cancels an unobserved request |\n| R-C2 | helper: `keepPrevious` in `vm.ts` keeps the old data only while the new key loads |\n| R-W1 | helper: `write()` publishes `pending` and `error` to the control (`console.store.ts`) |\n| R-W2 | helper: `write()` returns early while `pending` |\n| R-W3 | helper: the write's `done` callback invalidates the affected queries |\n| R-W5 | helper: `write()` drops an answer whose `epoch` is old |\n| R-W6 | not in the data layer: the shared order view offers Create return |\n| R-W7 | not used: no optimistic display |\n| R-B2 | helper: `app-view-block` gives way to the section's block state |\n| R-E1 | helper: a failed source shows its error where its data would be (`vm.ts`) |\n| R-E2 | built in: an observer of an errored key refetches it on re-observe (`Query.attach`) |\n| R-E3 | helper: a failed write keeps the user's input (`write()`) |\n| R-G1 | helper: a failed main source is its section's error (`block-state.ts`) |\n| R-G2 | helper: `failedCalls` names the failed source in the block |\n| R-G3 | helper: failures stay in their section stream (`vm.ts`, `withParts`) |\n| R-G4 | helper: `keepOnError` in `query.ts` keeps a polled value on failure |\n| R-G5 | helper: `retryCustomerSource` and `retryIfFailed` refetch only the failed keys |\n| R-G6 | helper: enrichment failures become notices on a ready section (`flag`) |\n| R-C3 | helper: `Query` keeps the value on a same-key reload (`stale` flag) |\n| R-C4 | built in: unsubscribing the in-flight request cancels it (`Query.detach`) |\n| R-W8 | helper: writes are not tied to a navigation (`write()` is outside the section streams) |\n| R-W9 | helper: the write's `error` keeps the input (`write()`) |\n| R-W10 | helper: `invalidate` on the affected queries and caches after success |\n| R-L1 | helper: `signedIn$` stops every poll and request at logout |\n| R-L2 | built in: cold observables, requested on subscribe |\n| R-L3 | helper: one `Entry` per key in `Query` |\n| R-L4 | built in: `debounceTime(300)` on the typed text and the editor search |\n| R-L11 | helper: sentence names are streams of their own, requested only for shown rows |\n| R-L9 | helper: `entity-cache.ts` collects ids per tick into batches of `MAX_BATCH` |\n| R-L10 | helper: one `EntityCache` slot per id |\n| R-L5 | helper: a settled `Query` entry stays cached for the session |\n| R-L6 | helper: public caches are not cleared by `clearSession()` |\n| R-L7 | helper: `invalidate` refetches a cached key only after a write |\n| R-L8 | helper: `pollMs` runs only while an observer exists |\n| R-P1 | built in: independent streams start in parallel and render on arrival |\n| R-P2 | built in: the in-flight orders list is a stream of its own |\n| R-P3 | helper: the order renders on arrival; names are `withParts` enrichments |\n| R-P4 | built in: a dependent request starts when its key arrives (`switchMap`) |\n| R-P5 | built in: a section with no input shows no data and no request |\n| R-P6 | helper: a cart line's price is its own stream, not joined with names |\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\nEight criteria, the same in every entry's README. Each is compared across the entries in [docs/contest/results](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/criteria.md); the numbers below come from there (line counts: card [06](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/06-boilerplate.md), Prettier-formatted, non-blank, non-comment).\n\n- **Eager or lazy start.** Lazy. An observable sends nothing until a view subscribes; the first observer of a `Query` key starts its request (`query.ts`, `attach`). Gives: a section that is not shown asks nothing. Costs: the rule \"load when not loaded, stale or errored\" is written here and must stay right.\n- **One request per key, and how long a value lives.** One `Entry` per key in a `Query`, one slot per id in `EntityCache`. A settled value lives until `clearSession()` (`sources.ts`); there is no eviction. Gives: no duplicate request. Costs: memory grows for the whole session.\n- **Cancelling a superseded read.** The last observer's `finalize` unsubscribes the in-flight request (`query.ts`, `detach`), and `switchMap` in the store takes the latest input. Gives: a late answer never reaches a newer view. Costs: the observer count is ours to keep right.\n- **Batching.** Ids requested in one tick are collected and split at `MAX_BATCH` (`entity-cache.ts`). Gives: batch endpoints are called in batches. Costs: the per-tick collection and the mapping of a failed batch back to its ids are our code.\n- **Keeping data on error or reload.** `keepOnError` keeps a polled value on failure; `stale` marks a key for refetch on the next observer; a failed enrichment is a notice on a ready section (`vm.ts`, `flag`). Gives: each case is explicit. Costs: three mechanisms for related behaviour.\n- **Boilerplate to add one value.** One more batched lookup like `tiers` costs 20 lines in 4 files. The data layer is 1668 lines: 429 generic, 166 per entity, 1073 domain. Costs: the value crosses four layers before a view sees it, and the generic part is the hand-built cache and batching.\n- **Where state lives.** One injectable, `console.store.ts`, owns every stream; components own none. Gives: one file shows the whole dataflow. Costs: that file is the largest in the entry and grows with each section.\n- **Dependency on a library.** RxJS only, already shipped with Angular. Gives: no library to upgrade. Costs: all the caching above is ours.\n\n## Try it\n\n- Turn on **Throw** on any service in the request panel above the demo: the\n  section fails in isolation, the rest of the page keeps working.\n- Set **API speed** to Slow, then switch customers quickly: the latest\n  selection wins, and the superseded read is cancelled.\n- Open the Cart tab, leave the page and come back: the tab preference is\n  remembered (R-S5); the customer and the open panel are not.\n- Log out while a request is pending: nothing of the session stays on screen,\n  and the late answer is dropped.\n";export{s as default};
